% Rust GGUF inspection module. Source: approved PRODUCT_INTENT and experiment plan.
% Use std IO and checked arithmetic. Expose inspect(path)->Gguf and read tensor methods.
<vocabulary>
duplicate: an identical metadata key or tensor name appears twice.
invalid: violates the version, count, type, shape, alignment or bounds checks listed in R-102.
</vocabulary>
<contract_rules>
R-101 (MUST): Parse little-endian GGUF v3 metadata and tensor descriptors, exposing architecture, alignment, data start, names, dimensions, storage types and offsets.
R-102 (MUST): Bound counts, nesting, strings, header size and tensor reads; reject truncation, invalid types, overflowing shapes/offsets, duplicate names, invalid alignment and overlapping tensor storage.
R-103 (MUST NOT): Write to an inspected input, execute model code, or allocate a whole checkpoint merely to inspect its metadata.
R-104 (MUST): Treat GGUF dimensions as fastest-axis first. Only unquantized BF16 tensors are eligible for the sparse editing workflow.
</contract_rules>
